1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
This lesson covers hand hygiene for fresh food areas. Clean hands are the single most important protection between our customers and foodborne illness, and the law requires every food handler to master this.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:30,000
First, when must you wash your hands? Always before starting your shift and before handling any food. Always after using the toilet, after breaks, after touching your face, hair or phone, after handling waste, and after handling raw meat, poultry or fish.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Now the technique. Wet your hands with warm running water and apply enough soap to cover both hands. Rub palm to palm, then the back of each hand, between every finger, around each thumb, and under your fingernails. This should take at least twenty seconds.

4
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Twenty seconds is longer than most people think. A simple trick is to count slowly to twenty, or hum a short song. Rushing the scrub is the most common handwashing mistake in food areas.

5
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Rinse thoroughly under running water and dry your hands with a single use paper towel. Never dry your hands on your apron or uniform. Use the towel to turn off the tap so your clean hands do not touch it.

6
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:38,000
What about gloves? Gloves protect food only when they are changed as often as you would wash your hands. Change gloves whenever you switch tasks, especially between raw and ready to eat food. Wash your hands every time you change gloves.

7
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Jewellery, nail polish and artificial nails trap bacteria and can fall into food. In fresh food areas, keep nails short, clean and unpolished, and remove watches, rings and bracelets before your shift. A plain wedding band is the only exception.

8
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:12,000
If you have a cut or wound on your hand, cover it with a blue detectable plaster and wear a glove over it. Blue is used because no natural food is blue, so a lost plaster is easy to spot before it reaches a customer.

9
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:28,000
To summarise: wash before food and after any contamination risk. Scrub for a full twenty seconds covering every surface. Dry with single use towels. Change gloves like you wash hands. And cover wounds with blue plasters. Your hands protect every customer we serve.
